            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0464" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">211.41/147</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-24">June 24, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        3.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 996</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction No. 1734, March 15 [<hi rendition="#italic">14</hi>],
                    1929 (File No. 211.41/137), relating to the Department’s conclusions and
                    suggestions on the draft of an extradition treaty, which was duly forwarded to
                    the Foreign Office under date of March 28, 1929, and to enclose a copy of a
                    Foreign Office note in reply, containing certain specific observations in regard
                    to the articles of the draft treaty.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray Atherton</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d369-a1.xml" xpointer="d369-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
